  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ins300.html",
  "prefLabel": "Ins 306.01 Purpose",
  "priorExpiration": "2009-02-16",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ins 306.01 Purpose. The purpose of this part is to provide standards for the disclosure of certain minimum information about annuity contracts to protect consumers and foster consumer education. The rule specifies the minimum information which must be disclosed, the method for disclosing it, and the use and content of illustrations, if used, in connection with the sale of annuity contracts. The goal of this rule is to ensure that purchasers of annuity contracts understand certain basic features of annuity contracts.\n\nSource. #2143, eff 1-1-83; ss by #4287, eff 7-1-87; ss by #5657, eff 7-1-93; ss by #7015, INTERIM, eff 7-1-99, EXPIRED: 10-29-99\n\nNew. #7450, eff 2-16-01, EXPIRED: 2-16-09\n\nNew. #12521, eff 4-28-18",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ins300.html"
